../../skills/security/SKILL.md:7:# NOTE 2026-07-29 : le bloc `paths:` a ete retire. Mesure par experience controlee
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:116:Apply every curated rule in `knowledge-base/domains/*/rules.json` to the target, mechanically:
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:119:For each rules.json across all domains:
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:128:1. **`detect.negative_patterns` are applied FILE-WIDE by the engine.** A broad negative such as `\$\{` suppresses the rule across any file containing a template literal — including genuine findings elsewhere in that file. Keep negatives narrow (annotation markers like `# local only`); push exclusion logic into the positive pattern instead. *(Measured 2026-07-29: `WEB-CRYPTO-002` initially missed a plaintext database password for exactly this reason.)*
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:129:2. **A rule carrying `detection_method: "semantic"` has empty patterns on purpose.** An absence — no auth middleware, no rate limiter — cannot be detected by matching a presence. Such rules are instructions for the agent pass, never mechanical matches. `WEB-AC-001` and `API-RESOURCE-001` were neutralised on 2026-07-29 after matching every Express route in existence.
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:130:3. **Attribute a finding only to a rule whose subject actually fits.** Proximity is not detection: crediting an oracle item to a rule that fired two lines away for another reason inflates recall. *(Measured the same day: a rate-limiting gap was briefly credited to a JWT rule and a CSRF rule firing on the same line.)*
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:132:Feed the resulting hit list into Step 2 as **prior findings**. Agents then spend model budget on what the rules could not reach — semantic gaps, business logic, cross-file data flows — instead of re-deriving what a regex already had.
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:175:      4. Use Read + Grep + Bash for KB pattern scanning (read rules.json, grep patterns, enrich via RAG)
../../skills/security/SKILL.md:195:**StopFailure hook** — if an agent fails due to API error (rate limit, timeout), the StopFailure hook should:
