   591	    "description": "A .env file carries live-looking secret assignments and is present in the working tree. If it is tracked by git, every value is in the repository history and must be treated as compromised — deleting the file does not remove it from history. Added 2026-07-29 after a benchmark showed no rule covered .env contents; WEB-CRYPTO-001 only matched secrets embedded in source files.",
